Concern: the issue observer describes the tensor a kernel receives whenever it cannot state a byte span
Upstream: not-submitted

0101 states an operand's `bytes` only when the tensor is one contiguous span: a strided view and a
plugin-private quantised tensor (a cube weight the kernel decodes in its own layout) both report 0
there, because neither has a byte count a consumer may read as one packed span. 0120 gives the
strided view its shape and strides, but only for a buffer, and not at all for a dtype with no byte
size -- so a consumer that must read a weight's or a pool operand's values has the declared shape
and nothing else. This extends the view to every operand the ABI cannot span: weights as well as
buffers, and a packed tensor of a dtype with no element size too. `bytes` stays 0 for those; the
view is the description and is never a synthesised packed copy. An element offset into a dtype with
no element size is not a byte address, so the view carries the offset as issued.

--- a/abi/rad_runtime.h
+++ b/abi/rad_runtime.h
@@ -936,7 +936,9 @@
-    /* The tensor the kernel receives, when it is not the declared one: a view narrows dim 0, or
-     * strides the last axis (the q norm reads the query half of the interleaved q|gate buffer).
-     * `view_off` is its first element's offset from the declared buffer's, and `view_stride` the
-     * strides into the declared layout. `bytes` is 0 for such a view: it is not one span. */
+    /* The tensor the kernel receives, when it is not the declared one: a view narrows dim 0, or
+     * strides the last axis (the q norm reads the query half of the interleaved q|gate buffer), or
+     * the declared dtype has no element size (a plugin-private quantised tensor, which the kernel
+     * decodes in its own layout). `view_off` is its first element's offset from the declared
+     * tensor's -- in elements, as issued -- and `view_stride` the strides into the declared
+     * layout. `bytes` is 0 for such a tensor: it is not one span a consumer may read packed. */
     uint8_t  view_rank;
     int64_t  view_shape[RAD_MAX_RANK];
     int64_t  view_stride[RAD_MAX_RANK];
--- a/core/runtime/issue.cpp
+++ b/core/runtime/issue.cpp
@@ -1368,13 +1368,16 @@
-        /* The view the kernel actually receives, when it is not the declared tensor; a consumer
-         * that has to copy the operand's values cannot read them as one span. */
-        if (full && o.kind == RAD_OPK_BUF && full->rank > 0 &&
-            !rad_tensor_is_contiguous(&t[i])) {
+        /* The tensor the kernel actually receives, when it is not one span of the declared dtype;
+         * a consumer that has to copy or read the operand's values cannot take them packed. A
+         * plugin-private dtype has no element size, so no span of it can be stated in bytes. */
+        if (full && (o.kind == RAD_OPK_BUF || o.kind == RAD_OPK_WEIGHT) && full->rank > 0 &&
+            (!rad_tensor_is_contiguous(&t[i]) || rad_dtype_bytes(t[i].dtype, 1) == 0)) {
             e.view_rank = (uint8_t)t[i].rank;
             for (uint32_t d = 0; d < t[i].rank && d < RAD_MAX_RANK; ++d) {
                 e.view_shape[d]  = t[i].shape[d];
                 e.view_stride[d] = t[i].stride[d];
             }
             const int64_t es = rad_dtype_bytes(t[i].dtype, 1);
             if (es > 0 && rad_dtype_bits(t[i].dtype) % 8 == 0 && t[i].data && full->data)
                 e.view_off = ((const uint8_t*)t[i].data - (const uint8_t*)full->data) / es;
+            else
+                e.view_off = o.offset;  /* no byte address: the element offset as issued */
         }
